WEBVTT

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:14.960
Global Astro!

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.780
Baby can I be? There's no future

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.220
You and me, full of scars

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.520
Let's look into the future

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.560
There's no end to everyone's song

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.760
That's what I believe

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.020
Oh yeah

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.060
How long will I pretend not to know?

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.320
Does it have to be?

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:29.900
Confirmed

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.910
I can't stop

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:31.450
I'm not in the mood

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:32.330
Even now

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.110
You miss me

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:33.790
That I know

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.870
So when you say

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:35.170
Answer

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.110
There's no such thing

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:37.850
I say that's something to find

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:38.450
I'm confused

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.450
What a person

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.070
Yes, yes, from here on out

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:42.590
Now

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:43.610
I'm going to follow you

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:44.510
Now

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:55.690
I'm here to see you

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:59.720
I'm here to see you

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.240
and flow to the end of your life

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.480
It's all for you

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.440
I'm talking to you like an artist

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.820
I'm such an artistic astro boy

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.660
Astro girl, everyone is exactly

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.780
Expo, Expo

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.420
And next, catch the future

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.640
To do so, let's go

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:19.020
Now, from the heart of the memories

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.340
Let's start again

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:28.700
Because I have it in my hands

00:01:36.908 --> 00:01:38.908
Thank you for watching!

00:01:41.484 --> 00:01:44.304
I did look around here, but...

00:01:45.068 --> 00:01:46.548
I won't give up.

00:01:46.892 --> 00:01:48.392
I'll definitely catch you.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:49.760
Hmm?

00:01:52.492 --> 00:01:53.132
That's it!

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.400
Kitty, come out here! Kitty!

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.510
Huh? Kitty, look!

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.000
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.130
Oh, I'm sorry. Are you hurt?

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.790
Who are you, old man? What are you doing in a place like this?

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.230
Hm? I'm Ban Shunsaku.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.230
I'm the great detective's bearded father.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.630
Well, this time it's a cat-searching job.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.310
What are you doing?

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.890
I'm looking for my mama.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.730
Hey, old man, I'm a detective!

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.160
Mama?

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.070
Five minutes left.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:39.540
I'm going to arrest Skunk tonight for sure.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.180
But he's so bold.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.240
Why would Skunk report a crime?

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.390
He's probably enjoying making the world go crazy.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.130
Yeah. The other day, he successfully reported his first crime.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:56.780
It was the theft of a pure gold nyorai from Kinsankaku.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:57.980
That's right.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:06.840
The storage room is a big gold mine with a heavy lead in the basement.

00:03:06.876 --> 00:03:07.956
There is only one entrance.

00:03:08.412 --> 00:03:12.412
As long as you keep an eye on it, you'll never be able to steal the pure gold Nyorai statue.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.340
That's impossible.

00:03:14.236 --> 00:03:15.256
But...

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:18.640
Hmm...

00:03:26.268 --> 00:03:29.988
suddenly disappeared from a room where no one was there.

00:03:30.412 --> 00:03:35.152
In other words, Skunk succeeded in committing an impossible crime.

00:03:35.276 --> 00:03:37.776
There was something wrong with the same-natured guard.

00:03:37.776 --> 00:03:39.076
It's about Stank.

00:03:39.076 --> 00:03:41.076
Maybe he was using a robot again.

00:03:41.356 --> 00:03:44.416
That's why we need the power of the atom.

00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:45.256
That's right.

00:03:45.548 --> 00:03:48.108
This time, we will do our best to guard.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.260
As expected of a skunk.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:51.200
Oh!

00:03:51.468 --> 00:03:52.328
I'm in trouble!

00:03:52.328 --> 00:03:54.408
It belongs to the Ministry of Science! Please let it pass!

00:03:54.764 --> 00:03:56.064
Dr. Ochanomizu?

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.140
Yuko-kun...

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.980
Leave this to Atom and go back to the Science Department immediately!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.630
There are a lot of documents to be paid for tonight!

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.630
Yuko-kun, umm...

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.710
Officer, we're in trouble!

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:07.090
Huh?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.810
What's wrong?

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:09.330
Huh?

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.710
What happened to the cash register monitor?

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.440
No, nothing special.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.240
That can't be!

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:21.700
B-but...

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:28.310
Officer, something huge is moving in the room!

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:28.730
What?

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:29.670
Huh?

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.370
Impossible! It's impossible to infiltrate!

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.450
Toidori, let's open the door and check it out!

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:36.720
Y-Yes!

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:56.130
Alright! We have to stop here!

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:56.670
Brother!

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.060
No way!

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:05.200
Where did that huge robot come from?

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:17.630
We've caught a suspicious man on the surface!

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:18.940
He must be a member of the Skunk!

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.660
Hey! Who do you think I am?

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.360
Detective Higeoyaji is talking about me!

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.900
Oh, Yu-chan! Just in time!

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:29.980
This stone head...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.860
Prove to everyone that I'm innocent.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.160
Uncle?

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:35.000
Huh?

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:36.670
Oh no!

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.990
I was so embarrassed because of you!

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:40.470
Why were you there?

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:43.450
Sorry, but I can't tell you.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:44.830
It's a secret investigation.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:46.430
What's a secret investigation?

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.110
You're going to sleep at home again.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:48.630
Yu-chan.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.050
Your angry face is getting more and more like your mother.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:53.930
Uncle, that's great.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.010
Hey!

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.930
Can you show me the scene?

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:00.920
Mom!

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:04.070
What the hell are you doing, you robot bastard?!

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.120
Uncle, please stop it already!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.420
Okay, okay. Don't get so angry.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:13.920
I'm in your way.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:19.940
Yuko-san, why are you getting so angry?

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.910
Uncle, you're a good person, but it's too late.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.730
That's why I don't like robots,

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:27.770
and they don't accept my work at the science school.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:31.800
Huh?

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.220
It's the effect of a powerful magnetic field, isn't it?

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:40.640
What I felt was also a special magnetic field.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.360
Maybe...

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:48.230
Don't get involved with the old man anymore.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:06.000
It's a mysterious giant robot. Is it really a ghost?

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.400
Ghost? You fool.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.080
There's always a trick to any mystery.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.640
Is a trick a serious case?

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.580
That's right. First of all...

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.100
Mr. Geoyaji, I have something to ask you.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.660
What's the use of a robot?

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.120
You came the day before yesterday.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:29.190
You're a tough robot.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:36.280
Heheheheh...

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:37.220
...jama, Wiro!

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:39.210
Oh, no, no!

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:45.470
Terumonka!

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:04.560
How is it? It's been a hundred years since I became a good-for-nothing.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:13.720
Here's your black coffee.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.800
Thank you.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.320
Oh, no. It's your win.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.740
You can't beat me, Atama.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.310
You can fight me again.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:24.740
Me, too.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.660
I lost.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.870
So, I...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:30.760
What do you want to hear?

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.100
The trick of the giant robot vanishing

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:35.090
About the powerful time

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:42.080
Look at that clean and beautiful town

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.740
New things are made from time to time

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:47.340
It has become a very convenient world

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:52.180
One-eyed Yu-chan says that robots are human friends

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:55.880
I can't get used to it

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:59.460
Mr. bearded doesn't like me either

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.780
I don't like robots at all.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.630
Oh, that's right.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:16.970
Atom, there's an interesting object in the middle of the fountain.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:22.850
That's a good idea.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:27.120
It seems to be the latest magnetic system.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:28.020
What?

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:36.850
Oh, what is that?

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:39.890
It's a new invention, a small-sized magnetic mechanism.

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:41.650
It's not announced to the world.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.260
Not announced to the world?

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.100
The developer's professor is missing.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:48.640
He was kidnapped by a villain.

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.160
Kidnapped?

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:54.700
A week ago, I met a boy named Sharaku in this park.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:58.350
My mother is a scientist studying magnetic mechanisms.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.260
That object was also made by my mother.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:02.800
Oh!

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.930
This is my amulet.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:11.720
Hmm? Is this also a magnetic mecha?

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.820
My mother gave it to me to keep it important.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.390
Please, Detective!

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:19.220
Help the kidnapped mother!

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:21.050
What did you say?

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:22.120
I'm aiming for a life!

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:26.560
The next day when I gave this to me,

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:27.800
My mother was gone.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:34.000
Don't cry. I'm sure I'll find it.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.670
I have nothing to say to the great detective.

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:40.960
I immediately began the investigation.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:45.990
And I finally came across an incident.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.640
The detective is always patient.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.420
As reported, Tsukanku stole the Junkyo Nyorai statue.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.120
The site is completely secret.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:00.970
We don't know how the culprit got in.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:06.380
And strangely enough, all the watches in the storage room are broken.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.510
We are currently investigating the relationship with the incident.

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:10.780
Broken watch?

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:14.540
Analog watches are easy to be affected by time.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:15.520
Huh?

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:29.240
It smells.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.880
I infiltrated the scene where the Nyoraizou was stolen.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.550
To verify the identity of the robot used in the crime.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:45.260
And the reasoning has changed to certainty.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.760
As I thought, there is a reason here as well.

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:54.860
There is no doubt. The identity of the unknown trick is a magnetic mecha.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:59.900
I see. That robot is...

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:02.570
It was a magnetic mechanism that divides into small parts.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:08.670
And the culprit who kidnapped Sharaku's mother is definitely a skunk.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:13.880
Amazing! Can you make me a assistant?

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:15.700
Assistant?

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:20.290
Holmes, Watson, Akechi Kogoro, and Kobayashi Shonen.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:21.960
A master detective doesn't need an assistant.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.120
A hard-boiled detective doesn't need an assistant.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:26.940
I need certain evidence.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.960
My analysis ability is...

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:33.100
Detective work is a series of trouble.

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.760
I'm always in a hurry and I have to be brave.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.470
I'm prepared for a half-baked.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.110
Immediately, Daichi.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.690
It's Yuko's air car.

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:45.830
Why did Yu-chan?

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:47.030
I forgot to put a regular contact.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:49.520
He came to look for me.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:52.220
It's a trouble if you get caught. I'm running away.

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:56.540
That's ...

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:06.220
Geez, what are you talking about, old man?

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:09.080
Atom is with an old man?

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.250
Yes. I'm sure he's helping out with the detective game.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.310
He's like a child to me. I'm troubled.

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:17.420
So, what was Atom like?

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:21.070
What do you mean? He seemed to be having fun.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.140
Then let's wait and see.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:26.160
It might be a good chance to get to know each other.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:27.860
Even for you, old man.

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:34.660
This drain pipe was connected to the underground duct of the tunnel.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.620
Look! The clock's hands are reacting.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:42.980
Maybe Skunk sent the magnetic mecha out of here.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:45.260
Atom, look at this map.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:50.630
The route of this magnetic mecha, and the previous one.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:55.320
The distance between the attack site and the entrance is almost the same.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:58.120
Skunk ran away from the site as much as possible.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:58.280
and committed the crime.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.760
If you do that, the probability of being found by the police will be low.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.280
In other words...

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:08.170
This line means that the distance between the two robots is close enough to control them remotely.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:12.110
If Skunk reports the location of the attack next time,

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:13.770
he might be able to identify the location.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:19.140
The Metro City Police is reporting the next crime.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:20.260
What?

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:25.520
Police officers, let's change our minds a little this time.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.130
We're going to give you a hint about the location of the attack.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:29.660
A hint?

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.810
In the middle of the four sticks, there is a place where a golden waterfall flows.

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:35.700
What does that mean?

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:39.380
I don't know. I'll think about it later.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.710
There's a waterfall in the middle of the sticks?

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:47.500
Is this what the four sticks mean?

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.540
Hmm. But where is the golden waterfall?

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:56.820
This is the golden waterfall!

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.750
Four sticks?

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:04.220
This looks like four sticks, doesn't it?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:05.410
It's an international casino.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:07.520
It seems that Skunk is aiming for it.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.860
But it has to be a golden waterfall.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:16.140
A golden waterfall!

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:17.450
There's no doubt.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.280
This is where he's aiming for.

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:21.930
Let's contact Detective Tawashi immediately.

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:28.300
Well then.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:29.970
Well then.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:30.640
I will give you the best prey.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:34.750
It's a gold coin worth 20 billion yen.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:43.560
Finally, the answer to the hint has been solved.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:45.590
But it's useless.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.210
From a small wind tunnel,

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:49.530
go straight to the underground gold mine.

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:59.870
Sire, using a robot for crime is the worst!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.560
Don't get me wrong. I love robots.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:07.000
Robots are more useful than humans, and above all, they're obedient.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:08.880
Right, Gadem?

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:15.500
Considering the route of the drain and the distance from the fire,

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.070
and the fact that they can't be seen,

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:22.140
the location of the Skunk must be around here.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:24.600
Now, Dr. Watto, it's your turn.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:25.940
Let Gadem go.

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:27.420
I refuse!

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:29.160
I told you this was the last time!

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.090
You don't know, do you?

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.240
You'll still have to earn money from now on.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:37.000
Or do you want to meet a cute boy with scary eyes?

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:41.000
I got it.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:46.360
Wait, the power limiter is not working.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.960
You can fix it right away, right?

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:51.350
Yes, if I change this circuit.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.120
What did you do?

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:56.610
I'll figure it out soon.

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:13.700
Get out of my way!

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:16.190
If this is all you've got, I'll take care of it.

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:26.320
Mr. Ryo, there's just a little bit of power leaking out of that truck.

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:27.990
You've got a good idea.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:28.990
Yeah.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.420
Call Detective Tawashi right now!

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:32.080
Yes, sir!

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.920
Oh, that's Sharaku's mother!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:36.480
What?

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:41.660
I'm counting on you, Gadem.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:53.890
I love robots, too.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:54.870
I can do this much.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:56.970
I can crush the traitor.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:02.130
Stop it!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:06.960
What are you doing here?

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:08.890
Kill him!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.700
What's with that old man?

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:18.860
He's a coward who's been fooled by a lot of people!

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:21.380
All right, I'll be waiting!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:23.090
What the hell are you doing?

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:26.300
The opponent is a magnet! Think about me!

00:18:36.268 --> 00:18:38.888
The enemy's potential energy is thousands of degrees.

00:18:38.924 --> 00:18:41.644
This Atom will melt away!

00:18:43.756 --> 00:18:44.756
The menu is Mio.

00:18:44.848 --> 00:18:47.348
Self-reliance is self-reliance! Switch on!

00:18:52.492 --> 00:18:54.032
I want to interfere with Adem's movements.

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:56.300
It stopped the heat dissipation to the Atom!

00:18:56.524 --> 00:18:58.764
That's what I'm talking about, you scum!

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:06.520
What the hell are you talking about?

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:25.200
Damn it! I have to stop the crane somehow in a little while!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.460
As long as I have that charm...

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:28.380
Charm?

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:28.980
Yes.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:32.900
I gave it to my son to initialize the self-destruction mecha, the anti-self-destruction unit.

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:35.870
This is my amulet.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:37.000
But...

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.880
Is this the main thing?

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.610
Eh? Why would you do that?

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:45.260
Alright, Atom!

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.030
Take this!

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:08.260
It's hard to get out of control!

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:10.700
It's hard to get out of control!

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:26.440
I'm going to kill you!

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:27.320
Shut up!

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:28.530
Wait!

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.150
You're not getting away!

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:39.230
Atom...

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:43.960
Atom, I'm glad you're safe.

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:46.550
Yes, I was able to save the dangerous place from Mr. Hideyoshi.

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.460
Mr. Hideyoshi must have hated robots.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.340
Why are you with Atom?

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:56.900
Well, in other words, a great detective needs an excellent assistant.

00:20:58.140 --> 00:20:58.660
Right?

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:02.820
Hehehehe.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:08.950
Thank you for your help. Thank you so much.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:11.040
Sara-kun! Sara-kun!

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.060
First of all, it's a pleasure.

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:22.130
When you have a useful tool,

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:24.650
people who abuse it will appear.

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:27.210
Like a skunk who uses robots.

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:29.640
It's annoying.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:34.260
But there are robots like you.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.310
I understand a little bit of what Yuko was saying.

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:41.340
See you, Atom. See you again.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:49.660
Is it so hard to say goodbye?

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:52.010
It's cute.

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:53.190
What?

00:22:00.476 --> 00:22:02.316
That's what I've done!

00:23:24.280 --> 00:23:24.700
Something's wrong!

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:27.530
The rescue team won't take off!

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:29.970
Aokishi, let's go with the robo-

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:30.850
Let's rescue them!

00:23:31.230 --> 00:23:33.890
Next time on Space Plant Crisis

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:35.330
Catch the Future with your heart!
